# Playwright MCP runtime dirs (one per server mode).
# Each mode's output/ is gitignored; the persistent mode's profile/ too.
# config.json, README.md, and a .gitkeep inside each dir stay tracked so the
# folder structure is visible on a fresh clone.
playwright/headless/output/*
!playwright/headless/output/.gitkeep
playwright/interactive/output/*
!playwright/interactive/output/.gitkeep
playwright/tracing/output/*
!playwright/tracing/output/.gitkeep
playwright/persistent/output/*
!playwright/persistent/output/.gitkeep
playwright/persistent/profile/*
!playwright/persistent/profile/.gitkeep

# Ephemeral modes use isolated (in-memory) profiles and should never write to
# their profile/ dir, but ignore any contents defensively so that if isolation
# ever regresses, captured cookies/credentials can't be committed. The
# placeholder README.md in each stays tracked.
playwright/headless/profile/*
!playwright/headless/profile/README.md
playwright/interactive/profile/*
!playwright/interactive/profile/README.md
playwright/tracing/profile/*
!playwright/tracing/profile/README.md

# Launcher runtime state (lockfiles, log) - per-mode subdir created on demand.
playwright/headless/state/
playwright/interactive/state/
playwright/tracing/state/
playwright/persistent/state/

## Web publish staging (intermediate dir assembled by tools/publish-web/build.ps1; Web/site/ IS tracked)
Web/_staging/

## Test rig (see TestRig/CLAUDE.md)
## The whole rig is DENY-ALL with a named allowlist, deliberately. Everything these
## tools produce is local-only, and several normal actions drop artifacts straight
## into the folder (snapshot -OutFile before.json, /screenshot?path=shot.png,
## scratch dumps). Deny-all means a stray artifact cannot be committed by accident;
## an ignore-a-few-things list would let every one of those through.
##
## The rig ROOT is deny-all too, for the same reason the halves are: a snapshot
## -OutFile with a relative path resolves against the shell CWD, and a run from
## the rig root would land the artifact here where an ignore-a-few-things list
## would wave it straight through. The allowlist is the one launcher, the shared
## lock and state-reset machinery, their test suites and the four docs. Every piece
## of live session state stays untracked: session.lock, session.dirty (the crash
## marker), session.state.json (the shared per-user snapshot) and baseline/ (the
## captured definition of a clean rig, including the config file contents it stores).
/TestRig/*
!/TestRig/CLAUDE.md
!/TestRig/MANUAL.md
!/TestRig/RESEARCH.md
!/TestRig/testrig.ps1
!/TestRig/testrig.tests.ps1
!/TestRig/lib/
!/TestRig/rig-lock.ps1
!/TestRig/rig-lock.tests.ps1
!/TestRig/rig-reset.ps1
!/TestRig/rig-reset.tests.ps1
!/TestRig/DedicatedServer/
!/TestRig/ClientRig/
!/TestRig/playtest/
!/TestRig/src/
!/TestRig/dev-plugins/
!/TestRig/testrig.exe

## The C# rig: source tree, and the committed AOT binary it produces.
##
## testrig.exe is build output and it IS tracked, so that a consumer never needs a
## dotnet build. The binary embeds a digest of this source tree and refuses to run
## when the two disagree, which is what keeps a committed artifact from going stale
## unnoticed. See TestRig/src/CLAUDE.md.
##
## Source only under src/: bin/ and obj/ are per-machine build output and would
## otherwise sail through the allowlist above.
/TestRig/src/**/bin/
/TestRig/src/**/obj/

## The merged BepInEx plugin, shared by both halves. Source only; its build output
## is deployed into each half's install tree, which is ignored wholesale.
/TestRig/dev-plugins/**/bin/
/TestRig/dev-plugins/**/obj/

## The one launcher's half-specific implementations. testrig.ps1 is the only entry
## point; lib/ holds the per-half function libraries it dot-sources. Source only,
## nothing generated, so a plain allowlist of the folder is enough.
/TestRig/lib/*
!/TestRig/lib/common.ps1
!/TestRig/lib/server.ps1
!/TestRig/lib/client.ps1

## Dedicated server half: local-only except source code under dev-plugins/, which
## carries its own README. install/ and data/ are ignored wholesale. Both the
## launcher and the half's manual used to live here; they are now
## TestRig/testrig.ps1 (server half in TestRig/lib/server.ps1) and TestRig/MANUAL.md.
/TestRig/DedicatedServer/*
!/TestRig/DedicatedServer/dev-plugins/
/TestRig/DedicatedServer/dev-plugins/**/bin/
/TestRig/DedicatedServer/dev-plugins/**/obj/

## Client rig half: local-only except source code under dev-plugins/. Its launcher
## and its three docs used to live here; they are now TestRig/testrig.ps1 (client
## half in TestRig/lib/client.ps1), TestRig/CLAUDE.md, TestRig/MANUAL.md and
## TestRig/RESEARCH.md. instances/ holds hard-linked copies of the game install and
## normally lives on the install's volume, not here; data/ holds the rig registry,
## per-instance manifests, settings, save roots, logs and PID files. Both are
## created on demand and both are covered by the deny-all above. A host instance
## writes its worlds under data/<instance>/userdata/saves/, which the deny-all
## already covers; nothing a host produces is ever committable.
/TestRig/ClientRig/*
!/TestRig/ClientRig/dev-plugins/
/TestRig/ClientRig/dev-plugins/**/bin/
/TestRig/ClientRig/dev-plugins/**/obj/

## Playtest harness: the library, its offline suite, the runner, its short manual and
## the per-mod checks under checks/. Deny-all inside here too, matching the halves: an
## evidence bundle normally lands in .work/, but -EvidenceRoot can point anywhere and
## a bundle carries every request and response of a run. Under an ignore-a-few-things
## list one of those would be committable by accident.
/TestRig/playtest/*
!/TestRig/playtest/CLAUDE.md
!/TestRig/playtest/playtest.ps1
!/TestRig/playtest/playtest-lib.ps1
!/TestRig/playtest/playtest-lib.tests.ps1
!/TestRig/playtest/checks/

